Area Network (WAN): A WAN spans large distances and connects multiple LANs or other networks together, often using public or private telecommunication links. Examples include the internet and private leased lines.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 - Metropolitan Area Network (MAN): A MAN c\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
overs a larger area than a LAN but smaller than a WAN, typically serving a city or a metropolitan region. It provides high-speed connectivity for organizations within the same geographical area.
