\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs28\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15998380\charrsid12152412 \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 - Bus Topology: In a bus topology, all devices are connected to a central cable (bus) in a lin
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 ear manner. Data transmitted by one device is received by all other devices on the bus.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 - Star Topology: In a star topology, all devices are connected to a central hub or switch. Data transmitted by one device is routed through the hub/switch to the intend\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 ed destination device.

\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 - Ring Topology: In a ring topology, devices are connected in a closed loop, with data flowing in one direction. Each device acts as a repeater to transmit the data to the next device in the ring.
