a. Hardware: This refers to the physical components of the IT system, including computers, servers, routers, switches, and other devices used to process and store data.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 b. Software: This e\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
ncompasses the programs, applications, and operating systems that run on the hardware and enable users to perform various tasks. Examples include word processing software, database management systems, and customer relationship management (CRM) software.

\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 c.\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
 Networks: Networks connect different devices within an organization, allowing them to communicate and share information. This includes local area networks (LANs), wide area networks (WANs), and the internet.
