\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs28\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15998380\charrsid12152412 \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
Information Systems (IS) refer to the broader framework that encompasses the management and use of information within an org\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
anization. It involves the processes, people, and technologies used to collect, organize, store, process, and disseminate information to support decision making and achieve organizational goals.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 Information Technology (IT) is a subset of Information System\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
s and focuses specifically on the technology infrastructure and tools used to manage information. IT deals with the hardware, software, networks, and data involved in the storage, retrieval, and transmission of information.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs28\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid2694819\charrsid10243499 \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 Data Flow Examples:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs28\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15998380\charrsid12152412 \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
a. Simplex Mode: In simplex mode, data can only flow in one direction. A common example is a television broadcast where the information is transmitted from the broadcasting station to the television viewers.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 b. Half Duplex: In half duplex mode, data can fl\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
ow in both directions, but not simultaneously. Walkie-talkies are an example of a half-duplex communication system where one party can transmit while the other party listens, and vice versa.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 c. Full Duplex: In full duplex mode, data can flow simultaneously\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
 in both directions. A telephone conversation is an example of a full-duplex communication system, where both parties can speak and listen at the same time.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 d. Asynchronous: In asynchronous data flow, data is transmitted in irregular intervals with the sen\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
der and receiver using start and stop bits to synchronize communication. An example is the transmission of data through email.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 e. Synchronous: In synchronous data flow, data is transmitted in a continuous stream without start and stop bits. Examples includ\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
e real-time video conferencing or live streaming where data is transmitted in real-time without interruption.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs28\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid15998380\charrsid10243499 \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 Four components of data communications system:
